@@ -15,3 +15,9 @@ Each task records `createdAt` and `updatedAt` as ISO-8601 date-time strings. A n
 matching timestamps. Completing, reopening, renaming, tagging or untagging a task updates `updatedAt`
 when the operation changes it. `createTodoList` accepts an optional timestamp function, which defaults
 to the current time, so callers can provide a deterministic clock when needed.
+
+Task input is validated when adding, renaming or tagging: titles must contain non-space characters
+and be at most 120 characters after trimming; priorities must be `low`, `normal` or `high`; tags
+must be non-empty and contain no whitespace. Tags supplied while adding a task follow the same rule.
+Invalid input returns an `invalid-input` error with a message describing the problem, and leaves the
+list unchanged. This keeps malformed values out of sorting and filtering operations.
